{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.PentagonUvCommutationWoronowicz","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.PentagonUvCommutationWoronowicz","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.pentagon_ascension_under_woronowicz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.pentagon_ascension_under_woronowicz","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L273-L305","doc":"**Pentagon-ascension precondition** (algebraic skeleton — derived).\n\nThe Faddeev–Kashaev pentagon identity for the quantum dilogarithm\n`Φ_q` applies to an operator pair `(Û, V̂)` precisely when they\n`q`-commute in the form `uv = q²·vu`.  This theorem discharges the\n*algebraic precondition* the pentagon rests on: under the Woronowicz\nleft-covariant calculus, **every** grade-1 element `q`-commutes with\nevery 1-form by the factor `q²`,\n`left_act x ω = q² • right_act ω x`.\n\nThis is the genuine computable content of the former `True`\nplaceholder, *derived* by specialising `q_commutation_grade_one` and\nuniversally quantifying over the grade-1 elements `x` and forms `ω`.\n\nThe remaining analytic content of the full corollary — the explicit\ntriple-absorption rule\n`Φ_q(|V_iV_jV_k|)⁽ⁿ⁾ = pair⁽ⁿ⁾ · Φ_q(|ÛV̂|)⁽ⁿ⁺¹⁾`, the\ngeometric convergence of the level-`(n+1)` residual\n(`prop:jet-tower-convergence`), and well-definedness of the\nall-orders mass tower\n`𝔪 = |Π V| + Σ_{n,S} z^{2(|S|-1)} Φ_q(|Π_{i∈S} V_i|⁽ⁿ⁾)` —\nrequires `Φ_q`, the brane-tower jet functor, and the convergence\ntheorem in Lean, all deferred.\n\n-- Ref: [faddeev_kashaev1994] Quantum dilogarithm\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:pentagon-uv-commutation ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.StandardHeckeWoronowicz.deg_generator_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.StandardHeckeWoronowicz.deg_generator_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L271-L271","doc":"Modular automorphism is the q-grading by Coxeter length:\n`to_calculus.deg σ_i = 1` for every Hecke generator `σ_i`\n(the Coxeter length of a simple reflection is 1).  This is the\nstandard modular automorphism on left-covariant Γ pulled back\nfrom `O_q(SU(N))` via Schur–Weyl–Hecke (`σ_q = q^{2·ℓ}`).\n\nEncoding the real claim (replacing the former `True` placeholder):\nevery generator sits in grade 1 of the q-grading, so its modular\nfactor is exactly `q²` (cf. `q_commutation_grade_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.StandardHeckeWoronowicz.generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.StandardHeckeWoronowicz.generator","kind":"def","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L261-L261","doc":"The Hecke generators `σ : ℕ → Hecke_n` (`σ i` is the generator\n`σ_i` of `H_n(R, q)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.StandardHeckeWoronowicz.to_calculus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.StandardHeckeWoronowicz.to_calculus","kind":"def","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L258-L258","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.StandardHeckeWoronowicz.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.StandardHeckeWoronowicz.mk","kind":"ctor","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L254-L254","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.StandardHeckeWoronowicz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.StandardHeckeWoronowicz","kind":"class","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L248-L271","doc":"Existence of the standard Woronowicz left-covariant calculus\non the Hecke algebra `H_n(q)`.\n\nStated as a class-instance hypothesis; constructing the concrete\ninstance is research-scale Lean work (port the 1989 Woronowicz\n+ 1991 Jurčo construction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.q_commutation_grade_one_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.q_commutation_grade_one_half","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L158-L182","doc":"Half-integer grading variant: for elements of grade `1/2`\n(= a single Hecke generator `σ_i^{±1}` in the GS filtration of\n`H_n(q)`), the modular factor is `q^1 = q`.\n\nThe half-integer grade is tracked by its double, `2·deg x = 1`,\nso the modular automorphism contributes the bare factor `q` (rather\nthan the `q²` of the integer grade-1 case): `Û·V̂ = q·V̂·Û`.\n\nThis is *derived* (replacing the former `True` placeholder): the\nleft-rule gives `left_act x ω = right_act ω (σ_q x)`, the grading\nlaw gives `σ_q x = q^(2·deg x) • x = q^1 • x = q • x`, and the\nR-linearity axiom pushes the `q` through the right action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.q_commutation_grade_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.q_commutation_grade_one","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L132-L155","doc":"Q-commutation theorem: under the Woronowicz left-rule, for any\nq-homogeneous element of grade 1 and any 1-form, left and right\nactions are related by a factor of q.\n\nThis is the operator-level content of `conj:pentagon-uv-commutation`\non the transient summand of the brane-tower descent involution\n(which projects out the descended `A_n` slot of `J^1(A_n)`,\nleaving only the `Ω¹(A_n)` slot — exactly where the bimodule\nrelation lives).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.instOmegaModule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.instOmegaModule","kind":"instance","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L125-L130","doc":"Expose the 1-form `R`-module structure as an instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.instOmegaAddCommGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.instOmegaAddCommGroup","kind":"instance","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L117-L123","doc":"Expose the 1-form module's additive structure as an instance so that\n`•` on `Ω` resolves in the theorems below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.right_act_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.right_act_smul","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L113-L113","doc":"R-linearity of the right action in its A-argument.  This is a\nbimodule axiom: scalars from R commute with the right\nmultiplication, so for any `r ∈ R`, `ω ∈ Ω`, `x ∈ A`:\n`right_act ω (r • x) = r • right_act ω x`.\n\nCloses the `sorry` in `q_commutation_grade_one` by giving the\nexplicit R-linearity needed to push `q^k` scalars through the\nright action.  Holds in any concrete bimodule (e.g. the\nstandard 4D Woronowicz calculus on `O_q(SU(2))`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.left_rule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.left_rule","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The LEFT RULE: bimodule actions are related by the modular\nautomorphism.  This is the defining axiom of the Woronowicz\nleft-covariant differential calculus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.sigma_q_grading_law","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.sigma_q_grading_law","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.sigma_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.sigma_q","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L95-L95","doc":"The modular automorphism σ_q(x) = q^(2 deg x) · x.\nDefined here as a hypothesis for the class user; in concrete\ninstances this is induced by the Woronowicz coproduct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.deg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.deg","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The q-grading on A (= GS filtration grade for QOU's Hecke algebra). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.right_act","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.right_act","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L89-L89","doc":"Right A-action on Ω. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.left_act","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.left_act","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L87-L87","doc":"Left A-action on Ω. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.omega_mod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.omega_mod","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Module structure on Ω over R. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.omega_addgroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.omega_addgroup","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L83-L83","doc":"Additive structure on Ω. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.Omega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.Omega","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The bimodule of left-covariant 1-forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PentagonUVCommutation.WoronowiczLeftCalculus","kind":"class","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pentagon-uv-commutation-woronowicz.lean#L56-L115","doc":"The brane-tower with Woronowicz left-covariant differential\ncalculus.  This is the §3b-cond class hypothesis closing\n`conj:pentagon-uv-commutation`.\n\nThe class abstracts:\n- `Omega n`: the bimodule of left-covariant 1-forms on A_n.\n- `left_act n` / `right_act n`: the bimodule actions, both\n  assumed `R`-linear in the `Omega` argument (additive bimodule\n  structure).\n- `deg`: the q-grading on A_n (= GS filtration grade in QOU).\n- `sigma_q`: the modular automorphism `x ↦ q^(2 deg x) · x`.\n- `left_rule`: the AXIOM `x · ω = ω · σ_q(x)` on left-covariant\n  1-forms — the defining property of the Woronowicz calculus.\n\nConstructing an instance for the QOU brane tower\n(`A_n = H_{n_0}(R, q)`) requires fixing a particular q-deformed\ndifferential calculus on the Hecke algebra; the standard choice\nis the bicovariant calculus pulled back from O_q(SU(n)) via the\nSchur–Weyl–Hecke duality, which has `σ_q = q^{2·ℓ}` where ℓ is\nthe Coxeter length.\n","signatureChunk":0}]}